{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016ZFHkK4svWHEjoR2xrCg9h","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Aurora\n2\t\n3\tThree nightly multi-agent sweeps that discover, validate, and catalog the\n4\topen-source Claude/agent ecosystem â€” Skills & Templates (23:00), Tools (00:00),\n5\tAgents (01:00). Outputs: a SQLite knowledge base, a browsable markdown library,\n6\tnightly executive summaries, an 08:30 morning briefing, and a `helping-hand`\n7\tplugin that surfaces matches from the library in any Cowork or Claude Code session.\n8\t\n9\tPlan and decisions: `..\\Skills and Agent\\Skills and Agent Tips\\NIGHTLY_SWEEP_PLAN.md` (v3).\n10\t\n11\t## Quick start (P1 scaffolding only â€” no live sweeps yet)\n12\t\n13\t```bash\n14\tcd C:\\dev\\aurora\n15\tpython -m venv .venv\n16\t.venv\\Scripts\\activate\n17\tpip install -e .[dev]\n18\tcp .env.example .env       # then edit .env with real keys\n19\tpython -m aurora.orchestrator --sweep skills --dry-run\n20\t```\n21\t\n22\t`--dry-run` walks the pipeline structurally (loads the seed map, registers a\n23\trun row with `status='dry_run'`, exercises each role's contract) but makes no\n24\tLLM calls and no network fetches. Use this to verify the wiring is correct\n25\tbefore P2 (first real sweep against a single seed).\n26\t\n27\t## Layout\n28\t\n29\t```\n30\taurora/\n31\t  orchestrator.py       entry point; --sweep {skills,tools,agents} [--dry-run]\n32\t  sweeps/               sweep-specific prompts & configs\n33\t  roles/                scout, quarantine, static_screener, runner,\n34\t                        critic_a, critic_b, reconciler, embedder, librarian\n35\t  kb/\n36\t    schema.sql          full v3 schema (Â§6 of plan)\n37\t    aurora.db           live SQLite database\n38\t    pricing.yaml        vendor pricing for cost estimation\n39\t    apply_schema.py     idempotent schema applier\n40\t  seed_map/\n41\t    skills.yaml         seeds for the 23:00 sweep\n42\t    tools.yaml          seeds for the 00:00 sweep\n43\t    agents.yaml         seeds for the 01:00 sweep\n44\t    quarantine/         shadow-mode seeds (3 nights before promotion)\n45\t  library/              human-browsable curated catalog (by-kind)\n46\t  reports/              nightly exec summaries + morning briefings\n47\t  prompts/              versioned prompt templates (SHA pinned per run)\n48\t  inspect/              cloned upstream repos for inspection (gitignored)\n49\t  sandbox/              ephemeral per-run scratch (gitignored)\n50\t  logs/                 transcripts + artifact bundles (gitignored)\n51\t  lock/                 file-based sweep mutex (gitignored)\n52\t```\n53\t\n54\t## Decisions locked in Â§17 of the plan\n55\t\n56\t| Item | Value |\n57\t|---|---|\n58\t| Runner sandbox | Docker (Docker Desktop) |\n59\t| Scheduler | Windows Task Scheduler (primary), Cowork mirror |\n60\t| Critic B | Gemini (primary), local OpenAI-compatible (fallback) |"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"71e5a556-8710-4d10-b60c-86fc91c9365e","uuid":"090af6aa-1f71-419a-8cc1-5c5305366256","timestamp":"2026-06-13T16:03:32.281Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\aurora\\README.md","content":"# Aurora\n\nThree nightly multi-agent sweeps that discover, validate, and catalog the\nopen-source Claude/agent ecosystem â€” Skills & Templates (23:00), Tools (00:00),\nAgents (01:00). Outputs: a SQLite knowledge base, a browsable markdown library,\nnightly executive summaries, an 08:30 morning briefing, and a `helping-hand`\nplugin that surfaces matches from the library in any Cowork or Claude Code session.\n\nPlan and decisions: `..\\Skills and Agent\\Skills and Agent Tips\\NIGHTLY_SWEEP_PLAN.md` (v3).\n\n## Quick start (P1 scaffolding only â€” no live sweeps yet)\n\n```bash\ncd C:\\dev\\aurora\npython -m venv .venv\n.venv\\Scripts\\activate\npip install -e .[dev]\ncp .env.example .env       # then edit .env with real keys\npython -m aurora.orchestrator --sweep skills --dry-run\n```\n\n`--dry-run` walks the pipeline structurally (loads the seed map, registers a\nrun row with `status='dry_run'`, exercises each role's contract) but makes no\nLLM calls and no network fetches. Use this to verify the wiring is correct\nbefore P2 (first real sweep against a single seed).\n\n## Layout\n\n```\naurora/\n  orchestrator.py       entry point; --sweep {skills,tools,agents} [--dry-run]\n  sweeps/               sweep-specific prompts & configs\n  roles/                scout, quarantine, static_screener, runner,\n                        critic_a, critic_b, reconciler, embedder, librarian\n  kb/\n    schema.sql          full v3 schema (Â§6 of plan)\n    aurora.db           live SQLite database\n    pricing.yaml        vendor pricing for cost estimation\n    apply_schema.py     idempotent schema applier\n  seed_map/\n    skills.yaml         seeds for the 23:00 sweep\n    tools.yaml          seeds for the 00:00 sweep\n    agents.yaml         seeds for the 01:00 sweep\n    quarantine/         shadow-mode seeds (3 nights before promotion)\n  library/              human-browsable curated catalog (by-kind)\n  reports/              nightly exec summaries + morning briefings\n  prompts/              versioned prompt templates (SHA pinned per run)\n  inspect/              cloned upstream repos for inspection (gitignored)\n  sandbox/              ephemeral per-run scratch (gitignored)\n  logs/                 transcripts + artifact bundles (gitignored)\n  lock/                 file-based sweep mutex (gitignored)\n```\n\n## Decisions locked in Â§17 of the plan\n\n| Item | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Runner sandbox | Docker (Docker Desktop) |\n| Scheduler | Windows Task Scheduler (primary), Cowork mirror |\n| Critic B | Gemini (primary), local OpenAI-compatible (fallback) |","numLines":60,"startLine":1,"totalLines":85}}}
