{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01NmgmLUyW59FjN6NbLWq5AK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the project docs, here's what Aurora is:\n\n**Aurora is an autonomous, multi-agent discovery-and-curation system for the open-source Claude/agent ecosystem.**\n\n- **Purpose â€” discover, validate, catalog.** It runs three nightly multi-agent \"sweeps\" that find, vet, and catalog open-source Claude/agent assets across three kinds: Skills & Templates, Tools, and Agents (`README.md:3-7`; CLAUDE.md \"Aurora at a glance\").\n\n- **How it runs â€” scheduled multi-role pipelines.** Each sweep is launched via `orchestrator.py --sweep {skills,tools,agents}` and pushes candidates through a chain of LLM-driven roles â€” scout â†’ quarantine â†’ static screener â†’ sanitizer â†’ runner â†’ critics (A/B/C) â†’ reconciler â†’ embedder â†’ librarian (`orchestrator.py:1-39`, `README.md:31-34`). Sweeps fire on Windows Task Scheduler (Skills 23:00, Tools 00:00, Agents shifted to ~22:00/01:00).\n\n- **What it ships â€” four artifacts + a plugin.** (1) a SQLite knowledge base (`kb/aurora.db`), (2) a human-browsable markdown library (`library/`, organized by kind), (3) nightly executive summaries plus an 08:30 morning briefing (`reports/`), and (4) a `helping-hand` Cowork/Claude Code plugin that surfaces library matches in any session (`README.md:3-7`, `README.md:45-51`).\n\n- **Distribution â€” two private repos.** A `publisher.py` step builds a scrubbed snapshot nightly (~01:45) and pushes it from the source repo (`aurora-source`) to a collaborator-facing distribution repo (`aurora-library`) (CLAUDE.md \"Key files\" / \"Aurora at a glance\").\n\n- **Cost-governed by design.** LLM calls funnel through `llm.py` with retry/degrade logic, and the orchestrator enforces per-sweep and per-role budget guardrails against monthly vendor caps (e.g. Anthropic $50, Gemini $10) (`orchestrator.py:52-60`).\n\n- **Current direction â€” an awareness/decision instrument.** Recent work (the \"awareness revamp,\" W2â€“W5 in git history; plan in `docs/AURORA_REVAMP_PLAN.md`) reframes Aurora from a pure catalog toward a read-only Flask dashboard and decision-grade reporting on the agentic fleet's value, health, and cost â€” not a rebuild (per memory `aurora-awareness-revamp.md` / `auroratwo-decision.md`).\n\nOne caveat worth flagging: `README.md` still describes \"P1 scaffolding only â€” no live sweeps yet,\" but the git history and plan docs show the system is well past that (live sweeps, publisher, dashboard all shipped) â€” so the README's quick-start framing is stale relative to actual state."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":920,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1243,"cache_read_input_tokens":34093,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1243},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"71e5a556-8710-4d10-b60c-86fc91c9365e","uuid":"2a4df9dc-1274-4955-82da-3d001d8cb28d","request_id":"req_011Cc1YNzqGJgPPY9MAYSyFN"}
